 :criteria
 {:construction
  "C11 construction criterion compiler/c11/semantic-mir-construction (Open): Construct the canonical target-independent MIR module/function/block/operation records from checked core, exposing control-flow and data-flow graphs and stable artifact identities. Cover the complete C11 families: constants/locals/block arguments; calls/tail calls/closures and direct/dictionary/vtable/dynamic dispatch; records/structs/tuples/enums/unions and field/index/slice/buffer operations; arithmetic/conversions; allocation/initialization/load/store/move/drop; region/arena and linear-resource lifecycle; branches/loops/matches and errors; FFI/host boundaries; atomics/locks/channels/tasks/synchronization; workflow suspension/resume/events; AI model/tool/memory/policy; domain anchors; runtime checks and proof/certificate references. Every operation has opcode, operands, result, type, effects/order, source/generated origin, profile and verifier status with applicable fact references; no-result operations use nil result and Unit or bottom as appropriate. Blocks have ordered operations and exactly one legal C11 terminator, including proof-qualified unreachable, profile-legal suspend/yield and legal tail call. SSA values or block arguments may represent joins, but public data-flow edges remain explicit. The module references actual checked core, profile, target request, functions/globals and metadata/anchor tables; functions retain parameters, return type, latent effects, entry/blocks and origin. A target request may constrain legality but cannot redefine opcode semantics. Required outputs: actual MIR/CFG/DFG, origin and anchor records plus operation-family/schema coverage fixtures under declared profiles. Reject malformed records/joins, missing required operation fields and target-specific instruction semantics in generic MIR with applicable C11-MODULE/BLOCK/TARGET-LEAK diagnostics. Positive construction produces verifiable artifacts, not a fabricated verifier success.",
  :facts
  "C11 fact-binding criterion compiler/c11/mir-fact-binding (Open): Before constructing admitted MIR, consume actual resolved/checked core and name/type/effect/profile/capability/ownership/safety products; unavailable required semantic facts cannot be deferred to a backend. Bind each module and operation to current source/compiler/module/pass identities and the applicable type, effect, ownership/lifetime, capability, safety-outcome, runtime-check, proof/certificate, source-origin, profile/target and domain-anchor tables. Safety-sensitive operations retain their check/proof/audited-unsafe references. A transformation preserves valid references or emits explicit invalidation/replacement records; stale references cannot be consumed until the required facts are regenerated and verified. Required outputs: actual fact/reference tables, operation-to-fact edges, invalidation/replacement and rejected-staleness fixtures. Accept fully bound checked inputs and correctly regenerated/reverified transformations; reject absent or mismatched core/fact/provenance, lost source/generated origin, stale proof/check/ownership or incompatible profile evidence with applicable C11-TYPE/EFFECT/SAFETY/ORIGIN/DOMAIN/VERIFY. Source obligations gravity/semantic-facts-before-mir and compiler/c11/mir-fact-binding share this input/reference boundary, not a new task. The actual upstream semantic producers retain their checks.",
  :ordering
  "C11 effect-order criterion compiler/c11/mir-effect-order (Open): Carry the actual effect set and required ordering constraints on each effectful operation and retain the corresponding semantic dependency edges. Accept transformations only with preserved or explicitly revalidated ordering; identical output values cannot justify silently reordered effects. Required outputs: operation/order graph and actual preserved/revalidated transformation fixtures. Reject a missing effect/order fact or an effectful reorder not permitted by the declared effect semantics with C11-EFFECT and the offending operation/source/fact context. Consume the actual Effect checker and transformation products without requiring whole-component completion.",
  :verifier
  "C11 verifier criterion compiler/c11/mir-verifier-gate (Open): Verify every block terminates, definitions dominate uses, operands/types match operation schemas, effect-order constraints are present, safety-sensitive operations have actual outcomes/check references, origins and profile constraints are valid, ownership/resource operations match C9 facts, runtime checks guard the intended operation, domain anchors are valid and target-specific opcodes occur only in target-lowering metadata. Required outputs: subject-bound actual verifier report, MIR diagnostic stream and accepted/rejected fixtures for every listed invariant, retaining module/function/block/operation, source span/origin, profile/target request, missing fact and remediation. Preserve C11-MODULE/BLOCK/DOMINANCE/TYPE/EFFECT/SAFETY/ORIGIN/DOMAIN/TARGET-LEAK/VERIFY code meanings. Positive fixtures verify valid typed/effected/safe MIR; every malformed-flow/fact/origin/profile/guard/anchor/target-leak fixture fails before optimization or target consumption. A metadata flag or syntactically present table is not an actual verifier result.",
  :serialization
  "C11 serialization criterion (Open): Round-trip actual module/function/block/operation records, explicit control/data-flow edges and shared metadata tables with deterministic identity and valid origin/provenance links. Preserve the domain anchor's domain/anchor ID, MIR operation links, external semantic artifact, equivalence-proof reference and fallback MIR subgraph for EFIR/schema/workflow/HDL/query/GPU anchors as applicable; a domain payload cannot replace its semantic anchor. Preserve fact invalidation/replacement hooks rather than silently renewing a stale table or proof. Required outputs: serialized MIR/table/anchor artifacts and actual round-trip identity/edge/invalidation comparisons. Reject lost or substituted table IDs, origins, graph edges, anchor/proof/fallback references or stale-state erasure with applicable C11-MODULE/ORIGIN/DOMAIN/VERIFY. This representation/identity contract does not make EML tree identity mathematical equality or independently validate a proof provider.",
  :consumption
  "C11 consumption criterion gravity/mir-verification-after-transform (Open): Run the actual MIR verifier after construction and after each transformation that may invalidate invariants. Bind each result to the exact current module, transformation and fact identities; reject failed, missing or stale verification before public Opt/Lower consumption. Required outputs: before/after MIR, actual verifier reports, preserved/invalidated/recomputed fact records and positive/negative consumer-gate results. Runtime checks remain safety-referenced MIR operations and generic dead-code elimination cannot remove them; check elision consumes the applicable checked PERF10 evidence with subject binding and proof/guard dominance, or retains the check/rejects. Exercise invalidating transforms, malformed flow/missing types/effects/safety/origins, invalid profile facts, invalid anchors, unchecked source/core/MIR delivery and bounds-check erasure without surviving proof. Target-family consumption also uses actual declared profile/target/runtime-provider support; the backend cannot legalize rejected MIR or redefine generic op semantics. The owning optimizer/lowerer and proof checker supply their actual products; MIR gate ownership does not implement them. Ordinary source editing and negative-fixture preparation do not require release or migration admission, and these future execution requirements confer no current implementation acceptance."},
 :task-count-delta 0,
